:: Bird Tower Brood
<<setTowerTemp>><<effects>>
<<npc "Great Hawk">>
<<bird_schedule>>
<<set _eggCount to nestEggCount()>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<if ["rest","brood","sleep"].includes($bird.activity)>>
		<<set $birdBrood to true>>
		You climb into the nest next to <<your_bird_text>>.
		<<if $bird.activity is "brood">>
			<<bHe>> opens one eye and <<if $monster is 1>>smiles at you before <<bhe>> <</if>>makes room. The two of you huddle around your <<pluralise _eggCount "egg">>.
		<<else>>
			<<bHe>> stirs lightly.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		You climb into the nest and sit cross-legged, carefully placing
		<<switch _eggCount>>
			<<case 1>>your egg
			<<case 2>>both of your eggs
			<<default>>all <<number _eggCount>> of your eggs
		<</switch>>
		in the gap.
	<</if>>
	<span class="blue"><i>Brooding will gradually make your eggs hatch faster.</i></span>
<<else>>
	You continue brooding with your <<pluralise _eggCount "egg">><<if $birdBrood is true>> and <<your_bird_text>><</if>>.
<</if>>
<<if $bird.state is "home" and ["rest","brood","sleep"].includes($bird.activity) and !$birdBrood>>
	<<set $birdBrood to true>>
	After a short while, <<your_bird_text>> hops into the nest next to you.
	<<switch $bird.activity>>
		<<case "rest">><<bHe>> snuggles up next to you to rest.
		<<case "brood">><<bHe>> huddles around the <<pluralise _eggCount "egg">> with you.
		<<case "sleep">><<bHe>> curls up with you and starts to drift off to sleep.
	<</switch>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<bird_pass 30>>
<<set _eggsNearHatching to 0>>
<<set _eggsCloseHatching to 0>>
<<set _eggsHalfHatching to 0>>
<<set _eggsFarHatching to 0>>
/* hatchDelay is per clutch, so brooding care is applied once per pregnancy. */
<<run T.eggsAtNest = getChildrenAt("tower").filter(child => childIsUnhatchedEgg(child))>>
<<run T.broodedPregnancies = []>>
<<run T.eggsAtNest.forEach(child => {
	if (!T.broodedPregnancies.includes(child.pregnancyId)) {
		T.broodedPregnancies.push(child.pregnancyId);
		addEggCare(child.pregnancyId, 2 * TimeConstants.secondsPerHour);
	}
})>>
<<run T.eggsAtNest.forEach(child => {
	const hatchDate = getHatchDate(getPregnancyOf(child));
	const hatchTime = new DateTime(hatchDate);
	if (Time.date.timeStamp >= hatchDate) {
		if (!V.eggsHatched) V.eggsHatched = [];
		V.eggsHatched.push(child.childId);
		T.readyToHatch to true;
	} else if (Time.date.compareWith(hatchTime).days <= 1) {
		T.eggsNearHatching ++;
	} else if (Time.date.compareWith(hatchTime).days <= 6) {
		T.eggsCloseHatching ++;
	} else if (Time.date.compareWith(hatchTime).days <= 11) {
		T.eggsOverHalfHatching ++;
	} else if (Time.date.compareWith(hatchTime).days <= 14) {
		T.eggsHalfHatching ++;
	} else {
		T.eggsFarHatching ++;
	}
})>>
<<if _eggsNearHatching>>
	<<if _eggCount gte 2>>
		<span class="teal"><<Number _eggsNearHatching>> of your eggs <<if _eggsNearHatching gte 2>>are<<else>>is<</if>> very close to hatching!</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="teal">Your egg is very close to hatching!</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if _eggsCloseHatching>>
	<<if _eggCount gte 2>>
		<span class="blue"><<Number _eggsCloseHatching>> of your eggs will hatch in a matter of days.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="blue">Your egg will hatch in a matter of days.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if _eggsOverHalfHatching>>
	<<if _eggCount gte 2>>
		<span class="pink"><<Number _eggsOverHalfHatching>> of your eggs <<if _eggsOverHalfHatching gte 2>>are<<else>>is<</if>> over halfway to their expected hatching time.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="pink">Your egg is over halfway to its expected hatching time.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if _eggsHalfHatching>>
	<<if _eggCount gte 2>>
		<span class="purple"><<Number _eggsHalfHatching>> of your eggs <<if _eggsHalfHatching gte 2>>are<<else>>is<</if>> about halfway ready to hatch.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="purple">Your egg is about halfway ready to hatch.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if _eggsFarHatching>>
	<<if _eggCount gte 2>>
		<span class="red"><<Number _eggsFarHatching>> of your eggs will still take a long time to hatch.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="red">Your egg will still take a long time to hatch.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>

<<if _readyToHatch>>
	You hear a tiny crackle from
	<<if _eggCount gte 2>>
		<<if $eggsHatched.length gte 2>>
			<<number $eggsHatched.length>> of your eggs. <span class="green">They're hatching!</span>
		<<else>>
			one of your eggs. <span class="green">It's hatching!</span>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		your egg. <span class="green">It's hatching!</span>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next (0:30)|Bird Tower Hatching]]>><<bird_pass 30>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $bird.state is "hunting" and $bird.timer lte 0 and !$possessed>>
	<<endevent>>
	<<npc "Great Hawk">>
	You hear the flap of wings as the <<beasttype>> returns.

	<<bHe>> lands and <<if $monster is 1>>walks<<else>>hops<</if>> over to you.
	<<unset $birdBrood>>
	<<bird_hunt_return>>
<<else>>
	<<endevent>>
	<<if $bird.state is "home" and !["rest","brood","sleep"].includes($bird.activity) and !$bird.override and !$birdBrood and Time.dayState isnot "night" and $bird.timer lte 0 and !$possessed>>
		<<npc "Great Hawk">>
		<<if $bird.injured gt 1>>
			<<set $bird.timer to 600>>
			You see <<your_bird_text>> sitting at the edge of the perch, looking out at the moor wistfully. It seems <<bhe>> wants to hunt, but <<bhis>> injury is still stopping <<bhim>>.
		<<elseif npcIsPregnant("Great Hawk") and talkedAboutPregnancy("Great Hawk","pc") and npcBellySize("Great Hawk") gte 12>>
			<<set $bird.timer to 300>><<set $birdBrood to true>>
			You see <<your_bird_text>> sitting at the edge of the perch, looking out at the moor. <<bHe>> seems to consider hunting for a moment,
			<<if $monster is 1>>
				but places <<bhis>> hands on <<bhis>> <<bellyDescription "Great Hawk">> and looks to you.
			<<else>>
				but wobbles in place for a moment, set off balance by <<bhis>> <<bellyDescription "Great Hawk">>.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<<bHe>> instead joins you in the nest, snuggling up against you.
		<<elseif $bird.injured is 1>>
			<<set $bird.timer to random(30, 60)>>
			<<set $bird.state to "hunting">>
			You watch <<your_bird_text>> leap from the perch. It seems <<bhe>> wants to hunt, but didn't want to disturb you. <span class="green"><<bHis>> wing must be fully healed.</span>
		<<else>>
			<<set $bird.timer to random(30, 60)>>
			<<set $bird.state to "hunting">>
			You watch <<your_bird_text>> leap from the perch. It seems <<bhe>> wants to hunt, but didn't want to disturb you.
		<</if>>
		<<endevent>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Keep brooding (0:30)|Bird Tower Brood]]>><<transform bird 1>><<trauma -3>><</link>><<ltrauma>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Get up|Bird Tower]]>><<unset $birdBrood>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Bird Tower Hatching
/* ============ 번역 필요 ============== */
<<setTowerTemp>><<effects>>
You watch as the <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "egg continues" "eggs continue">> to shake, small hairline cracks forming along the top.
<br><br>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<if $bird.state is "hunting">>
		<<set $bird.state to "home">><<set $bird.timer to random(45, 120)>>
		After a few minutes, <<your_bird_text>> flies in through the open wall, <<if $bird.upgrades.decor gte 3>>pushing the curtain aside and <</if>>landing beside you.
		<<if $monster is 1>>
			<<bHis>> eyes widen. "Glad I made it in time!"
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<switch $bird.activity>>
			<<case "brood">>
				<<your_bird_text "cap">> gives the <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "egg">> some room, but looks like <<bhes>> barely managing to contain <<bhis>> excitement.
			<<case "sleep" "rest">>
				<<your_bird_text "cap">> stirs, <<bhis>> eyes slowly opening. <<bHe>> barely has time to process what's happening, but quickly stands up and looks over the <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "egg">> with excitement.
			<<case "bathe">>
				<<your_bird_text "cap">> leaps from the rainwater pool and rushes over. <<bHe>> barely has time to process what's happening.
			<<default>>
				<<your_bird_text "cap">> hurries to your side. <<bHe>> barely has time to process what's happening.
		<</switch>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	<<bHe>>
<<else>>
	<<your_bird_text "cap">>
<</if>>
begins to poke at the shell, but stops <<bhimself>>.
<<if $monster is 1>>
	"Children must be strong enough to get out on their own." <<bHe>> leans down. "Come on, little <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "one">>. Come say hello. We've been waiting for you."
<<else>>
	<<bHe>> starts to coo at the <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "egg">>, encouraging the <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "baby">> to emerge.
<</if>>
<br><br>

The top of <<if $eggsHatched.length gte 2>>one of the eggs<<else>>the egg<</if>> breaches.

<<childSelect $eggsHatched[0]>>
<<if $childRecords[$eggsHatched[0]].features.monster is "monster">>
	A surprisingly human face greets you, using <<childhis>> tiny hands to push away the broken edges of the egg. <<childHe>> trills as <<childhis>> eyes slowly open for the first time, beholding <<childhis>> parents.
	<br><br>

	<<childHe>> continues to push out of the egg, trying to get to you. <<childHe>> gets halfway out before the egg tips over, tumbling the rest of the way. <<childHis>> wings are nothing but two strands of muscle and skin protruding from <<childhis>> back, not having developed feathers yet. Despite this, you can't help but find beauty in your child.
<<else>>
	A tiny beak peeks through, widening the hole. The face of a baby bird greets you as <<childhe>> keeps pushing. <<childHe>> trills as <<childhis>> eyes slowly open for the first time, beholding <<childhis>> parents.
	<br><br>

	<<childHe>> continues to push out of the egg, trying to get to you. <<childHe>> gets halfway out before the egg tips over, tumbling the rest of the way. <<childHe>> is almost entirely pink, having not yet developed feathers or pigmentation. Despite this, you can't help but find beauty in your child.
<</if>>
<<if $eggsHatched.length is 2>>
	<<childHis>> sibling's egg soon breaches as well, revealing a very similar sight.
<<elseif $eggsHatched.length gte 3>>
	<<childHis>> siblings' eggs soon breach as well, revealing very similar sights.
<</if>>
<<bHe>> wraps a wing around you, and you snuggle into <<bhis>> plumage. <br><br>
<<if $bodysize lte 1 and $monster is 1>>
	<<bHe>> leans over slightly and rests <<bhis>> head atop yours.
<<elseif $monster isnot 1 and $bodysize gte 3>>
	<<bHe>> nuzzles <<bhis>> head under your chin, resting it on the front of your shoulder. <</if>>The two of you spend a minute or two like that, just enjoying being with each other. <<lstress>>
<<bird_pass 15>>
<br><br>

<<if $monster is 1>>
	"Welcome to life, Little <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "Hawk">>." <<your_bird_text "cap">> seems to be on the verge of tears. As much as you find the name 'Little Hawk' endearing, you should come up with <<if $eggsHatched.length is 2>>proper names<<else>>a proper name<</if>>.
<<else>>
	<<your_bird_text "cap">> nudges the <<pluralise $eggsHatched.length "newborn">> with a tenderness unbefitting <<bhis>> large frame and intimidating silhouette. <<bHe>> lets out a low coo, seemingly content.
<</if>>
<<endevent>>
<br><br>

<<hatchUi "tower" "Bird Tower Hatching 2" 20>>

:: Bird Tower Hatching 2
<<setTowerTemp>><<effects>>
<<childSelect $eggsHatched[0]>>
당신은 <<if $eggsHatched.length is 2>><<childrenNames $eggsHatched>>에게서<<else>><<childname>>에게서<</if>> 마지막 알껍데기 조각을 조심스럽게 떼어낸다. <<if $eggsHatched.length is 2>>그들은<<else>><<childHe>>【은는】 <</if>>너무나 연약하고 부서질 것 같아 보인다.
<br><br>

<<npc "Great Hawk">>
<<if $monster is 1>>
	<<your_bird_text "cap">>【은는】 <<if $eggsHatched.length is 2>><<childrenNames $eggsHatched>><<else>><<childname>><</if>>【을를】 감상하며 당신을 날개로 감싼다. "고맙소, <<wife>>. 당신 덕분에 정말 행복하오."
<<else>>
	<<your_bird_text "cap">>【은는】 <<if $eggsHatched.length is 2>><<childrenNames $eggsHatched>><<else>><<childname>><</if>>【을를】 감상하며 당신에게 몸을 비빈다.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $syndromebird isnot 1>>
	<span class="red"><i>자신만의 새끼를 부화시킨 후, 당신은 거대 매가 그저 짝을 원했을 뿐이라는 것을 깨닫는다.</i> 당신은 "스톡홀름 증후군: 거대 매" 특성을 얻었습니다.</span>
	<br><br>

	<<loveInterestAdd "Great Hawk">>
	<br><br>
	<<set $syndromebird to 1>>
	<<unset $birdescaped>>
	<<run delete $bird.syndrome>>
	<<specialClothesUnlock "set" "bird">>
<</if>>

<<set $bird.activity to "rest">>
<<set $bird.timer to 30>>

<<link [[다음|Bird Tower]]>><<endevent>><<unset $eggsHatched>><<unset $eggsMoved>><</link>>
<br>

:: Bird Tower Forcefeed Insist
/* ============ 번역 필요 ============== */
<<effects>>

<<if $phase is 0>> /* Scold */
	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"I-I'm really not that hungry," you say, curling up around your rumbling stomach.
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		"There's no way I'm eating that thing," you say, ignoring your rumbling stomach.
	<<else>>
		"I can't eat that," you say, even as your stomach rumbles.
	<</if>>
<<else>> /* Do nothing */
	You turn your head away, ignoring the way your stomach rumbles.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $monster is 1>>
	The <<beasttype>> frowns. "<<Wife>> needs to eat," <<bhe>> says, tearing a piece off the creature with <<bhis>> talons.
	<<if playerIsPregnant() and playerNormalPregnancyType() is "hawk" and talkedAboutPregnancy("pc","Great Hawk")>>
		"Need to feed eggs so they can grow healthy."
	<<else>>
		<<if $phase is 0>> /* Scold */
			"Even if you don't like it, <<wife>> shouldn't starve."
		<<else>> /* Do nothing */
			"Do you know how to eat? Do I need to feed you myself?"
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	There's a desperate edge to <<bhis>> voice as <<bhe>> thrusts the meat in your face.
<<else>>
	The <<beasttype>> lets out a <<= understandsBirdBehaviour() ? "mournful croon" : "quiet noise">> before <<bhe>> picks the creature back up and tears a piece off with <<bhis>> beak. <<bHe>> chirps <<= understandsBirdBehaviour() ? "insistently" : "repeatedly">> as <<bhe>> hops closer, trying to put the meat directly in your mouth.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Eat|Bird Tower Forcefeed]]>><<set $phase to 0>><<set $hunger to 1>><<transform bird 1>><<bird_stockholm 1>><<npcincr "Great Hawk" love 1>><</link>><<gbirdstockholm>><<glove>><<lllhunger>>
<br>
<<link [[Refuse|Bird Tower Forcefeed Refuse]]>><<bird_stockholm -1>><<npcincr "Great Hawk" love -1>><</link>><<lbirdstockholm>><<llove>>
<br>

:: Bird Tower Forcefeed Refuse
<<effects>>

당신은 원하지 않는다며 고개를 젓는다.
<br><br>
<<= $monster is 1 ? '"먹어, <<wife>>," <<beasttype>>【이가】 고집한다' : "<<beasttype>>【은는】 계속 지저귄다">>. <<if $monster is 1 or understandsBirdBehaviour()>>점점 좌절하며<</if>> 고기를 당신 입에 직접 쑤셔 넣으려고 한다. 당신이 <<bhim>>【을를】 밀쳐내자 <<bhe>>【은는】 갑자기 비명을 지르며 생물을 떨어뜨리고 당신을 잡으려 한다.
<br><br>
<<athleticsdifficulty 1 800 true>>
<<if $athleticsSuccess>>
	<span class="green">당신은 몸을 숙인다.</span> 당신이 탑 뒤쪽으로 허둥지둥 도망치는 사이 <<bhis>> 발톱이 등을 스치며 아슬아슬하게 빗나간다. 벽에 난 구멍으로 <<= $bodysize gte 3 ? "간신히 몸을 욱여넣는다" : $bodysize gte 2 ? "기어 들어간다" : "굴러 들어간다">>. <<beasttype>>【은는】 비명을 지르며 구멍을 할퀸다<<= $bodysize gte 3 ? ". 당신이 다리를 빼내기 전에 다리를 긁히고 만다.<<pain 8>><<ggpain>>" : ". <<bHe>>【은는】 이 안까지 닿지 못하지만, <<bhis>> 발톱이 돌에 남긴 깊은 홈을 보면 별로 위안이 되지 않는다.">><<stress 6>><<trauma 6>><<gstress>><<gtrauma>>
	<br><br>
	<<beasttype>>【이가】 포기할 때까지 당신은 숨은 곳 뒤쪽에서 몸을 떤다. <<bhis>> 발톱이 물러나고 그 자리에 <<bhis>> 얼굴이 나타난다. 커다란 눈 하나가 <<= $monster is 1 or understandsBirdBehaviour() ? "슬프게" : "뚫어지게">> 당신을 바라본다.
	<<if $monster is 1>>
		"<<Wife>>?" <<beasttype>>【이가】 부드럽게 말한다. "미안하오. <<= $bodysize gte 3 ? "다치게 할" : "겁줄">> 생각은 없었소. 준비되면 먹으시오."
	<<else>>
		<<beasttype>>【은는】 <<if understandsBirdBehaviour()>>미안한 듯<</if>> 울음소리를 낸다. <<bhe>>【은는】 <<bhis>> 머리 깃털을 납작하게 붙이고 땅에 바싹 엎드린다<<if understandsBirdBehaviour()>>. 덜 위협적으로 보이려는 듯하다<</if>>.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	대답을 기다리지 않고, <<beasttype>>【은는】 찢어진 생물을 남겨둔 채 뒤로 물러선다. <<tearful>> 당신은 다시 열린 공간으로 기어 나온다.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[다음|Bird Tower]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	피하려고 했지만, <span class="red"><<beasttype>>【은는】 너무 빨랐다.</span> <<bHe>>【은는】 당신을 땅으로 덮쳐 폐에서 숨을 몰아내고, 온 체중으로 당신을 짓누른다.<<pain 4>><<gpain>>
	<br><br>
	당신은 <<bhim>> 아래에서 발버둥치지만, 영양실조 상태에서는 저항할 힘이 없다.<<tiredness 10>><<stress 6>><<ggtiredness>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<beasttype>>【은는】 당신이 지치기를 기다리는 동안, 생물을 다시 집어 들고 체계적으로 찢기 시작한다.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[다음|Bird Tower Forcefeed]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<set $hunger to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Bird Tower Forcefeed
<<effects>>

<<if $phase is 0>> /* Eat */
	당신은 체념하고 <<beasttype>>【이가】 입에 고깃덩이를 넣어주도록 내버려 둔다. 질기지만, 별다른 맛은 나지 않는다. 이상한 온기가 몸을 채운다. <<eatLurker>><<drugs 120>><<ggdrugged>>
	<br><br>
	<<beasttype>>【은는】 당신이 먹는 것을 보고 기뻐하며, 한 입 크기로 생물을 열심히 찢어 계속 먹여준다. <<bHe>>【은는】 당신이 씹는 속도보다 거의 더 빠르게 먹여주다가, 당신이 더 큰 조각에 목이 막히기 시작하자 속도를 늦춘다. <<bHe>>【은는】 잠시 당신을 걱정하다가, 당신이 간신히 삼키자마자 다른 조각을 입술 너머로 밀어 넣는다.
<<else>> /* Refuse */
	<<bhe>>【이가】 당신이 발버둥을 멈춘 것을 확인하자, <<beasttype>>【은는】 당신의 입을 억지로 벌리고 목구멍으로 고깃덩이를 밀어 넣는다. 당신은 질식을 피하기 위해 반사적으로 삼킨다. 이상한 온기가 몸을 채운다. <<eatLurker>><<drugs 120>><<ggdrugged>>
	<br><br>
	당신이 삼키자 <<beasttype>>【은는】 만족스러운 소리를 내며, 또 다른 조각을 당신의 입술에 갖다 댄다. <<if $monster is 1>>"그래, 어서 먹어."<</if>>고개를 돌려보려 하지만, <<beasttype>>【은는】 당신이 체념하고 <<bhe>>【이가】 계속 먹이도록 내버려 둘 때까지 <<bhis>> 공격 각도를 조절할 뿐이다. 굴욕적이지만, <<bhim>>【을를】 막을 방법은 없다.<<stress 6>><<trauma 12>><<gstress>><<ggtrauma>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
곧 당신의 배가 가득 차고, <<beasttype>>【은는】 <<= $phase is 0 ? "물러난다" : "당신을 풀어준다">>.
<<if $monster is 1>>
	"그렇게 나쁘진 않았지?" <<bhe>>【이가】 당신을 훑어보며 묻고는, <<bhis>> 깃털을 부풀리고 돌아선다. "<<Wife>>【은는】 다음 건 <<pherself>> 먹을 수 있겠지."
<<else>>
	<<bHe>>【은는】 날카로운 시선으로 당신을 훑어보더니, <<bhis>> 깃털을 부풀리고는 만족한 듯 돌아선다.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $bird.syndrome gte 15>>
	<<bhe>>【이가】 그러자, 당신은 자신도 모르게 <<bhim>>에게 손을 뻗는다. <<bHe>>【은는】 잠시 멈춰 당신을 돌아보고, 당신은 순간 감정에 휩싸인다. <<bHe>>【은는】 <<bhis>> 나름의 방식으로 당신을 돌보려고 무척 애쓰고 있다. 다른 어디에서 이런 친절을 느껴본 적이 있었던가? 당신이 굶지 않도록 이렇게까지 애쓴 사람은 아무도 없었다. 고아원에서는 분명 아니었다.
	<br><br>
	당신은 더 가까이 다가가 온 힘을 다해 <<beasttype>>【을를】 껴안는다. <<beasttype>>【은는】 놀라서 울음소리를 내더니, 이내 <<bhis>> 날개로 당신을 부드럽게 감싸 안는다.
	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"먹여줘서 고마워요,"
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		"그건 끔찍하진 않았어,"
	<<else>>
		"먹을 거 줘서 고마워,"
	<</if>>
	<<beasttype>>의 깃털에 파묻혀 약간 웅얼거리며 말한다.
	<br><br>
	<<if $monster is 1>>
		"천만에, <<wife>>." <<beasttype>>【이가】 당신의 머리 위에 <<bhis>> 턱을 올리며 말한다.
	<<else>>
		<<beasttype>>【은는】 대답으로 지저귀며, 당신의 등 위로 <<bhis>> 머리를 기댄다.
	<</if>>
	당신은 한동안 그렇게 <<bhim>>의 포옹을 즐기다가, 마침내 놓아줄 시간이 된다. 당신이 <<beasttype>>【을를】 놓아주자 <<beasttype>>【은는】 작게 지저귀며, 당신의 <<= $monster is 1 ? "발톱" : "부리">>【을를】 <<bhis>> <<= $harpy gte 4 ? "깃털" : "머리카락">>【으로로】 가볍게 빗어준다. 당신은 뒤로 물러서며 미소 짓는다.

	<span class="red">이건 <<bhis>> 잘못이 아니야. <<bHe>>【은는】 그저 짝을 원할 뿐이야.
	<br>
	스톡홀름 증후군: 거대 매 특성을 얻었습니다.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<loveInterestAdd "Great Hawk">>
	<<set $syndromebird to 1>>
	<<unset $birdescaped>>
	<<run delete $bird.syndrome>>
	<br><br>
	<<specialClothesUnlock "set" "bird">>
<</if>>

<<link [[다음|Bird Tower]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Bird Loft 1
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "orphanage">><<effects>>
고아원에 도착한다.
<br><br>
<<if Time.hour gte 7 and Time.hour lt 9>>
	먼저 안으로 들어가니, 베일리가 아직 <<nnpc_his "Bailey">> 사무실에 있는 게 보인다.
	<br><br>
	베일리가 아직 있는 동안에는 아무것도 지을 수 없다. 공사 소리가 너무 시끄러울 테고, <<nnpc_hes "Bailey">> 분명 눈치챌 것이다.
	<br><br>
	<<set _passTime to "<<passTimeUntil 9>>">><<set _passTimeDisplay to "0:" + ("0" + ((45 - Time.minute + 60) % 60)).slice(-2)>>
	<<link [[기다린다|Bird Loft 2]]>>_passTime<<set $phase to "wait">><</link>>
<<else>>
	먼저 안으로 들어간다. 베일리의 모습은 보이지 않는다. 안도의 한숨을 내쉬며, 인부들에게 따라오라고 손짓한다.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[다음|Bird Loft 2]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Bird Loft 2
<<effects>>

<<if $phase is "wait">>
	인부들에게 일을 좀 미뤄야 할 것 같다고 말한다. 그들은 별다른 불평 없이 동의한다. <<person3>><<person>>【이가】 동료들과 이야기를 나누며 아침 식사를 먹기 시작한다. 함께 자리에 낀다. 꽤 즐겁다.<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<person>>【이가】 계란 요리를 다 먹을 즈음, 저 멀리서 베일리의 차가 떠나는 게 보인다.
	<br><br>
	이제 방해될 게 없으니, 인부들에게 안으로 따라오라고 말한다.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
계단을 올라 그들을 이끌고, 몇몇 고아들 옆을 지나친다. 아이들이 호기심 어린 눈으로 당신을 쳐다본다.
<br><br>
다락으로 통하는 문에 다다라, 줄을 당겨 다락으로 이어지는 사다리를 내린다. 먼저 위로 올라가고, <<person1>><<person>>【와과】 <<person2>><<person>>【이가】 뒤따라 올라온다. 나머지 둘은 사다리 옆에 남아 필요한 도구들을 옮겨준다.
<br><br>
주위를 둘러보며, 개조하기 적당한 창문이 어디일지 살핀다. 마을이 보이는 쪽 창문은 너무 눈에 띄기 때문에 고를 수 없다. 그러다 보니 숲이 보이는 창문만 남는다. 조금 넓혀야 할 것 같고, 이왕 하는 김에 완전히 새로운 모습으로 바꿔볼 생각이다.
<br><br>
<<person>>에게 뒤쪽 창문을 퇴창으로 바꾸고 싶다고 말한다. <<He>>【은는】 고개를 끄덕이고는 작업에 들어간다.
<br><br>

<<link [[다음 (0:10)|Bird Loft 3]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>

:: Bird Loft 3
<<effects>>

그들은 손발을 맞춰 작업한다. <<person1>><<person>>【이가】 망치로 쇠지렛대 머리를 나무 틀에 박아 넣고 벽에서 떼어내기 시작한다. <<person2>><<person>>【이가】 반대쪽에서 같은 작업을 한다. 틀이 낡아서 큰 저항 없이 떨어져 나온다.
<br><br>
소음 때문에 관심이 쏠리고, 곧 아래층에서 몇몇 머리가 삐죽 올라온다. 누가 다치기라도 할까 걱정되어 아이들을 쫓아내는 동안, 아이들은 웃고 소리 지르며 도망 다닌다.
<br><br>
<<person3>><<person>>【와과】 <<person4>><<person>>【이가】 창문 꼭대기까지 닿도록 사다리를 들고 올라온다. 뜯어낸 목재 조각들이 구석에 쌓여간다. 마지막 부분이 떨어져 나가자, 인부들은 몇 가지 안전 조치를 취한 뒤 유리를 틀에서 조심스레 떼어내 옆으로 옮긴다.
<br><br>
둘은 새 유리와 교체용 부속을 가지러 다시 자리를 뜬다. 그 사이, <<person1>><<person>>【이가】 공구함에서 톱을 꺼내 벽을 잘라내며 구멍을 넓히기 시작한다. <<He>>【은는】 이따금 멈춰서 이 정도면 충분히 넓은지 물어보고, 당신이 고개를 저으면 다시 톱질을 이어간다.
<br><br>
작업이 끝날 무렵, 뒤쪽 벽면의 공간은 이전보다 거의 세 배는 넓어져 있다. 여러 사람이 둘러앉기에 충분한 크기다.
<br><br>

<<link [[다음 (0:20)|Bird Loft 4]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>

:: Bird Loft 4
/* ============ 번역 필요 ============== */
<<effects>>

The <<person3>><<person>> arrives with the new trims. The colour matches the orphanage walls, though the wood is far sturdier and more refined.
<br><br>
The workers spend far longer reinforcing the widened opening than they did removing the old window. Extra beams are hammered into place beneath the sill, followed by angled supports to bear the weight of the bay jutting from the wall.
<br><br>
The <<person4>><<person>> arrives later with the panes of glass. They pause their work to go downstairs and carry each panel back up.
<br><br>
<<if $physique gte ($physiquesize / 7) * 5>>
	You lend them a hand, <span class="green">making work a little easier.</span> They appreciate the gesture.
<<else>>
	You try to help, <span class="red">but they shoo you away,</span> worrying that you might drop and break the glass.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Once the glass panels are all brought up, they return to assembling the frame. The center piece goes in first, with the side windows attached at shallow angles. Two workers hold the structure steady while the <<person2>><<person>> nails and braces it into the wall, checking repeatedly to make sure the projection remains level before the glass is finally installed.
<br><br>
The workers seal the edges and hammer the last strips of trim into place. By the time they step back from their work, the old wall has transformed into a broad bay window jutting proudly from the orphanage.
<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	<<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		Rain covers the fresh glass,
	<<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
		Moonlight pours through the fresh glass,
	<<else>>
		The fresh glass reveals the dark night outside,
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		Rain covers the fresh glass,
	<<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
		Sunlight pours through the fresh glass,
	<<else>>
		The fresh glass reveals the cloudy weather outside,
	<</if>>
<</if>>
scattering across the dusty floorboards.
<br><br>
The orphans crowd the window, overlooking the forest. The view is beautiful. Vast green patches seem to stretch far beyond the skyline.<<ggghope>><<hope 10>>
<br><br>
The work's done. You thank the workers and escort them out.
<br><br>
You return to the loft to examine the newly installed bay window. It's finally taking shape, but you feel something is missing. It would look less dull with some decorations.
<br><br>

<<if $money gte 100000 and Time.dayState isnot "night">>
	<<link [[Buy decorations (0:20) (£1000)|Bird Loft Decor 1]]>><<money -100000 "BayWindowDecor">><<pass 20>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<span class="blue">You can buy decorations once you have enough money.</span>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[다음|Orphanage Loft]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Bird Loft Decor 1
<<effects>><<set $loft_gh to 3>>

고아 몇 명을 데리고 쇼핑센터로 향한다.
<br><br>
여러 가게를 돌며 커튼, 이불, 누비이불, 베개, 쿠션을 산다. 고아들이 짐 나르는 걸 도와준다. 진열대를 지나다 은은한 소리에 귀가 쏠린다. 윈드차임이다. 그것도 산다.
<br><br>
고아들이 신이 나서 지나치는 가게마다 들르자고 조르는 바람에, 예상보다 훨씬 오래 걸린다. 아이들은 새로 산 물건들을 한아름 안고 집으로 돌아오는 내내 재잘거리며 신나게 뛰어논다.
<br><br>
계단을 올라 다락으로 들어가, 장식품들을 내려놓는다. 이제 당신이 일할 차례다.
<br><br>

<<link [[장식하기 (1:00)|Bird Loft Decor 2]]>><<pass 60>><</link>><<housekeepingdifficulty 400 1000>>

:: Bird Loft Decor 2
/* ============ 번역 필요 ============== */
<<effects>>

You set up the hanger for the curtains first. The window is very tall. There's no ladder around so you decide to stack a stool on a chair to reach the top of it. The orphans stick around to help you, and hold your footing steady.
<br><br>
<<if $housekeepingSuccess>>
	<<pass 10>>
	<span class="green">You are good at this,</span> and it doesn't take long to finish the work. You climb down with the help of the others.
<<else>>
	<<pass 30>>
	<span class="red">You have a hard time figuring out what to do.</span> You wobble while trying to secure and hang the curtains. The orphans hold onto your footing with effort.
<</if>>
<br><br>
With the hardest part finished, the only thing left is decorating the space into a cosy resting place.
<br><br>
You spread the duvets on the windowsill first, then add layers of quilts on top. Then, you add the cushions and pillows to the sides, covering the hard corners.
<br><br>
You open the biggest window in the middle, attaching the hook onto the roof, and hanging the wind chime up. A breeze goes by, carrying the fresh scent of the forest, making the chime ring with a melodic tune.
<br><br>
You step back to admire your work. It looks nice and soft, tempting you to jump right in. The orphans cheer.<<trauma -20>><<llltrauma>>
<br><br>

<<link [[다음|Orphanage Loft]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
